    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i manage a rental property in phoenix and one of the tenants is complaining that the ac is running all the time but her master bedroom stays really hot compared to the rest of the house. what are some common reasons this happens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "One common reason for uneven AC performance across a rental property is inconsistent airflow or sealing issues around the AC unit. Leaks or gaps in the ductwork or air handler can cause cooled air to escape, resulting in warmer temperatures in some areas. Another possibility is that the AC's temperature settings might be inconsistent, with the bedroom thermostat set too low or unevenly distributed throughout the house. Additionally, issues with insulation or window seals can also impact cooling performance in specific areas.",
